   * Three cases are the exception and can still print a Python error trace: Ctrl-C, running out of memory and a closed output pipe.
+    Text nested too deeply (about 30,000 levels) used to be a fourth: every place that reads JSON now goes through one
+    reader (`src/lead_desk/jsonread.py`) that turns it into a plain refusal, and `tests/test_r7c_one_json_loader.py`
+    fails if any file parses JSON another way.
   * A key file that is empty, longer than 4096 characters, has more than one line, or holds a space, a control character or a character outside printable ASCII is refused at start with a fixed message (the key text is never printed).
   * Network and protocol faults (a bad address, a cut-off answer, a reset) print only a short fixed error text (never
     the name of the error type, the address or a header).
